    "q-164373": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164373",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Identify the surface ${z}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $a=b=c=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
