    "q-164551": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164551",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Identify the surface $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}+4x+8z-10=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4{z}^{2}+4x+8z-10 & =0 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}+2x)+{y}^{2}-4({z}^{2}-2z)-10 & =0 \\\\ 2[(x+1)^{2}-1]+{y}^{2}-4[(z-1)^{2}-1]-10 & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)^{2}-2+{y}^{2}-4(z-1)^{2}+4-10 & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}-4(z-1)^{2}-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}-4(z-1)^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}-4(z-1)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(-1,0,1).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
